WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Narrator] Donald Trump is
the first former president

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.510
to be charged with a crime,

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.480
but he isn't the first
former presidential candidate

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.740
to be indicted

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.010
or for that indictment to
involve a hush-money payment.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.330
Just over 10 years ago,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.640
Democrat John Edwards
stood trial for money

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.710
and gifts given to his mistress.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.990
- There's nothing illegal about
giving somebody hush-money

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:19.920
not to talk about it.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.040
If it was done specifically
for the purpose

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.700
of promoting your candidacy
for a federal office,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.590
that's where the problem comes in.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.480
- [Narrator] Here's how
the two cases compare

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.820
and what we can learn about
the potential strengths

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.690
and weaknesses of the one
against Trump from the other.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.630
Let's start with what
happened with John Edwards.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.340
A senator from North Carolina,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.830
he became John Kerry's 2004 running mate

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.620
before running in the
2008 presidential primary

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.350
against Barack Obama and Hillary Clinton.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.380
He did okay in Iowa but
quickly dropped out.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.800
- It's time for me to step aside

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.710
so that history

00:01:00.369 --> 00:01:01.560
can blaze its path.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.450
- [Narrator] That year,
tabloid stories surfaced

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.880
about him having a child from an affair,

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.280
which, after two years of denying,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.260
- Tabloid trash is full of lies,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.670
- [Narrator] He admitted to.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.350
The scandal had everything.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.480
- Could be the biggest
political sex scandal

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.410
of our generation.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.030
- I just turned to him
and said, "You're so hot."

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.070
- [Journalist] Hundreds of
thousands of dollars given

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.270
to him by supporters.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.310
- [Anderson] Private jet
flights and luxury hotel rooms.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.714
- [Journalist] While his wife
was battling terminal cancer.

00:01:25.714 --> 00:01:29.070
- [Journalist] John Edwards'
sex tape details revealed.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.200
- It was a huge scandal at the time.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.700
People loved Elizabeth Edwards.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.650
Elizabeth Edwards really helped

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.930
John Edwards' reputation mammothly.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.660
So they really sold
themselves as, you know,

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.200
a loving, everyday American family.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.760
- [Narrator] Here's what
the Justice Department said

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.320
happened during the campaign.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.060
Campaign worker Rielle Hunter,

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.590
pregnant with John Edwards' daughter

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.410
while his wife, Elizabeth,
was dying of cancer,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.200
was given cash, luxury
hotel stays, apartments,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.780
and rides on private
planes by a wealthy member

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.090
of his campaign and a wealthy donor

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.530
to be kept out of sight.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.570
These were also given to a close aide,

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.300
who falsely claimed to
be the baby's father.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.090
None of this money came
directly through the campaign

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.710
or Edwards himself.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.160
Prosecutors argued Edwards
orchestrated this web of money

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.190
and that the payments were
made to help his campaign.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.200
A federal grand jury indicted Edwards

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.710
on six federal counts of
campaign-finance law violations.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.750
- John Edwards is a lousy human being,

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.850
but I think this is a really lousy

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.650
and flimsy criminal case.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:29.790
- [Narrator] Melanie Sloan founded

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.500
this government accountability group

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.930
and still works in ethics in campaign law.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.850
She followed the Edwards trial closely.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.683
- There was no evidence

00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:38.490
that John Edwards
personally gave the money.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.490
Regardless of whether that had happened,

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.920
there still would've been
the question about why.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.260
Is the money a campaign donation?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.080
Is it being spent to
advance your candidacy

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.870
or is it money being spent to hush this up

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:55.770
for some other reason, I.e.
to protect your family?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.890
- While I do not believe
I did anything illegal

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.800
or ever thought I was
doing anything illegal,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.030
I did an awful, awful lot that was wrong.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.130
- [Narrator] New York
prosecutors argue, with Trump,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.730
the reason was clearly
because of the 2016 election.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.710
Trump denies any wrongdoing.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.260
Here's what prosecutors say happened.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.620
In 2016, porn star Stormy
Daniels' lawyer went

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.630
to the "National Enquirer,"

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.550
yes, that same tabloid,

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.160
to sell her story about an
alleged sexual encounter

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.350
with Trump from a decade prior.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.080
The CEO of the tabloid's
publisher, David Pecker,

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.930
was able to connect her with
Trump's lawyer Michael Cohen,

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:38.040
who eventually paid her
$130,000 to keep quiet.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.130
Cohen was later reimbursed by
submitting monthly invoices

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.450
for legal services,

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.450
which were paid by Trump
through the Trump Organization.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.820
New York prosecutors say
those payment records

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.710
were false business records.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.390
- [Melanie] The 34 charges come out

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.890
of the same set of facts.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.390
Each time there's an invoice

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:55.740
and each time there's a payment

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.810
and each time there's
a bookkeeping record,

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.170
that is all the crime of
falsifying the business records

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.810
in order to cover up a crime.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.070
- [Narrator] With Edwards' case,

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:08.160
this donor had died and this one was 100

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.840
and never testified.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.790
A jury acquitted him on one charge

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.860
and deadlocked on another five.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.140
So, the trial ended in a mistrial.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:18.750
Jurors said there wasn't
enough evidence tying him

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.583
to the money.

00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:21.360
- We all though that he knew,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.360
but there just was not the
evidence there to prove it.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.850
- It was just a lack of evidence.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.560
- [Narrator] With Trump, prosecutors say

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.380
they have evidence that he
was involved in the payments,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.110
besides Trump's name and
signature on the checks,

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.880
and that the intent of the payments

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.890
was to help his campaign.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.980
Cohen has already pleaded
guilty and served time in jail

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.800
for these payments being campaign-related.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.990
And prosecutors say Trump directed Cohen

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.470
to delay Daniels' payment
until after the election,

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.030
because then, it would not matter

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.010
if the story becomes public.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.590
Prosecutors also point
to a similar payment made

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.500
to another women, who alleged
she had a sexual encounter

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.390
with Trump, Karen McDougal.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.400
They say Pecker and
Cohen worked out a deal

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.200
that ultimately paid McDougal
$150,000 for her silence

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.080
and that there are audio
recordings of Trump and Cohen

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.000
discussing this arrangement.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.520
Testimony from Pecker says
he made the connections

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.700
to the two women to ensure
no damaging allegations

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.710
would be published before the election

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.380
and thereby influence that election.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.870
- The indictment and statement
of facts particularly

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.940
do not suggest in any way, shape, or form

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.700
that this was ever about
hiding it from his wife.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.800
In fact, they make it very, very clear

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.050
that what they wanna do is
hide it during the course

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.880
of the presidential election.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:36.990
- [Narrator] Federal prosecutors,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.210
when charging Cohen on 2019,

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:42.510
declined to indict Trump,
who was still in office.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.750
These charges were filed
in a New York State court.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.060
Experts like Sloan argue that this case

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.790
may not even be as strong
as the one against Edwards,

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.680
which was in federal court,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.330
even with these connections.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.310
- I don't think this is
a slam dunk by any means.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.470
The fact that it's not
being a federal case,

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.700
that it's actually not being done

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.690
by the Justice Department

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.460
when you have a federal
campaign-finance law

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.860
and that it's being
bootstrapped into a state court,

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.600
that is unprecedented.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.690
- [Narrator] Trump pleaded
not guilty to all 34 charges.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:12.510
He denies the alleged sexual encounters.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.150
- This fake case was
brought only to interfere

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.493
with the upcoming 2024 election.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.277
And it should be dropped
immediately, immediately.

00:06:21.277 --> 00:06:22.350
(crowd applauding)

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.750
- [Narrator] He's not likely
to face jail time if convicted

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.700
and the trial, if it happens,

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.440
isn't expected to move quickly.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.384
The next court date is
in December of 2023.

00:06:31.384 --> 00:06:34.717
(light music continues)

